at in the trailer looked  ridiculous like the lady gaga costumes  that everyone in the capital wears it  works in a school that helps build this  really big really interesting world the  performances are also spot on I already  knew Jennifer Lawrence  was a good actress but she's got just  sheer presence and incredible subtle tea  here she conveys an awful lot by doing  an awful little and it's that's a really  hard thing to pull off and she nails  that so well and she's supported by a  great cast as well many whom are capable  of doing that same thing Woody Harrelson  great example Donald Sutherland does  very little but conveys so much you've  got some more over-the-top performances  as well but they're great to wes Bentley  gives a good performance for the first  time since American Beauty Stanley Tucci  is always great in everything it doesn't  matter if the movie sucked or not he's  always great Elizabeth Banks she really  surprised me just because her character  is so aggressively shallow it's really  kind of amazing just across the board  incredibly well cast very well performed  and I actually want to single out the  sound design and the music on this thing  I like good sound work but I'm not an  audio file but the sound design on this  thing is incredible and so much is  conveyed with those sounds some of the  hits that are delivered in the fight  they're brutal and they're brutal  because of the sound design and other  things as well the sound when katniss  draws that bone those metal arrows  scrape against the bow that is a  signature sound and the music to it  often plays against what you expect from  many of the scenes that it's used in but  that all plays very well into the  atmosphere of the film as much as this  film surprise me on a lot of levels now  I'm definitely glad i saw it it's not  perfect remember that fantastic world I  talked about well it's so good that when  the actual hunger games themselves start  it feels a little bit like a step back  because the Hunger Games the competition  where these all these teenagers have to  fight it out to the death takes place in  the woods and the woods could be  anywhere in any timeframe and you lose  all the flavor uniqueness of the world  that we've just been with for the first  hour thankfully we still get little  touches up because it flashes back and  we see woody harrelson still negotiating  for things for his team and you see the  different districts you know viewing the  games as they were going so we touch  back in that world but the actual hunger  games themselves probably the least  interesting part of the movie it's not  bad ness  but another thing that the games  themselves have working against it is  the camera work there's a lot of very  unnecessary shaky cam in this and  sometimes it works when it's a more  low-key up so that you just get that  handheld feel the cameras just bobbing a  little bit it so it makes it feel a  little more intimate and that's fine but  as soon as the action scene starts the  camera starts doing this and it makes  the action scenes difficult to follow  the main reason I'm able to follow the  action scenes at all is because of that  brilliant sound design I mentioned but  the camera work itself is distracting  it's not as offensive as these things  can be i've seen some movies that are so  bad with the shaky cam I just I can't  even watch them is this isn't that bad  but it's not good and I wish they hadn't  done it I suspect part of the reason  they do it is to be able to secure a  pg-13 rating because if these fights  were filmed any more clearly this thing  would probably have to be rated R which  would alienate the main demographic you  know the people actually read the books  so it may have been as much a logistical  decision as a stylistic one but it just  still annoys me and there are a couple  of story aspects that don't play as well  as they probably should have and I think  they're probably really only there  because they were such an important part  of the book there's a character I'm not  even gonna name this character because I  think I might end up getting getting too  much indisposed with that but there's a  character who it seems very obvious from  the way this character is used that they  are very big in the book and very  important in the book and they're  important in certain aspects in this but  they don't appear a lot so when this  character eventually gets paid off the  film it kind of banks too much on that  payoff and it doesn't feel earned I'm  sure it probably works very well in the  book the problem when the movie is it  was already two hours and 20 minutes  long and for this payoff to of work  right that you probably would have  needed at least in another 15 minutes  with this character specifically for the  payoff to work as well as they're trying  to make it there's some other nitpicky  things although the CGI didn't work for  me also the fire looked really fake and  I mean that both in terms of the fake  fire that's on the close of the  characters as well as the real fire that  goes on in the forest at one point  there's some creatures at the end they  they  wonky thankfully they're kept in  darkness that helps a little bit but for  something that was hype this much and  had the budget that I'm sure this thing  had I would I was expecting a little bit  more solid special effects work but you  know these are minor quibbles and this  thing just it really surprised the heck  out of me and now I gotta go and see the  next one before the third one comes out  so let me ask you this what's the movie  that had been hiked up for you and you  were sure I'm not really gonna enjoy  this you went to see it and it turned  out to be way better than you thought it  was going to be give me an example let's  share let's talk about it until next  time this council is adjourned
 

